GRA-19 -- kgraphCost isolated-anchor handling was dead, and the naive fix double-counts
=======================================================================================
kgraph_cost.c searched for an isolated anchor with a loop whose body was
`if (degree != 0) continue;' -- both outcomes continue, so domnnum always ended
at domnnbr and the `if (domnnum != domnnbr)' block (which freezes isolated
anchors at their own load) never ran. Empty parts of a band graph therefore got
an *average* load target they can never reach.

Just turning the search into `== 0) break;' (the review's one-word fix) is not
enough: the final loop then recomputes comploadavg for ALL domains, including the
isolated anchors the block already handled, subtracting their share twice. The fix
also skips isolated anchors in that final loop.

Reproducer gra19.c builds, via kgraphBand(), a band graph around a 2-part mapping
of a 16x16 grid onto cmplt(4) in which parts 2 and 3 are empty, so their anchors
are isolated (degree 0, load 1):
  cc.sh <build> GRA-19/gra19 GRA-19/gra19.c ; LD_LIBRARY_PATH=<build>/lib ./GRA-19/gra19
  pristine 7.0.17 : band avg 65 65 65 65   dlt 64 64 -64 -64   (block dead: empty parts get an average share)
  patched         : band avg 129 129 1 1   dlt  0  0   0   0   (block live: empty-part anchors frozen at load 1)
Both keep sum(dlt)=0; the patched targets are the physically meaningful ones.
